 #: src/appendix/tone-mapping-tutorial.xml:216(para)
 msgid ""
 "The image in Figure 4 clearly has “blown” highlights in the sky. But the "
 "highlights aren’t really blown (that is, clipped to 1.0 in one or more "
 "channels). Instead the highlight information is still there, but the RGB "
-"channel values fall outside the RGB <ulink url=\"https://"
-"ninedegreesbelow.com/photography/display-referred-scene-referred.html\"> "
-"display channel value</ulink> range of 0.0f to 1.0f. The sample points "
-"dialog in Figure 4 above shows four sample points that have RGB channel "
-"values that are greater than 1.0. As shown in Figure 5 below, adding a mask "
-"allows you to recover these highlights by bringing them back down into the "
-"display range."
-msgstr ""
+"channel values fall outside the RGB <ulink "
+"url=\"https://ninedegreesbelow.com/photography/display-referred-scene-"
+"referred.html\"> display channel value</ulink> range of 0.0f to 1.0f. The "
+"sample points dialog in Figure 4 above shows four sample points that have "
+"RGB channel values that are greater than 1.0. As shown in Figure 5 below, "
+"adding a mask allows you to recover these highlights by bringing them back "
+"down into the display range."
+msgstr ""
+"Bilden i figur 4 har tydligt ”utbrända” högdagrar i himlen. Men högdagrarna "
+"är inte verkligen utbrända (det vill säga klippta till 1,0 i en eller flera "
+"kanaler). Högdagerinformationen finns i stället kvar, men RGB-kanalvärdena "
+"faller utanför intervallet 0,0f till 1,0f för RGB-<ulink "
+"url=\"https://ninedegreesbelow.com/photography/display-referred-scene-"
+"referred.html\">visningskanalvärden</ulink>. Provpunktsdialogrutan i figur 4"
+" ovan visar fyra provpunkter med RGB-kanalvärden större än 1,0. Som figur 5 "
+"nedan visar kan en mask återställa högdagrarna genom att föra tillbaka dem "
+"till visningsintervallet."
 
 #: src/appendix/tone-mapping-tutorial.xml:230(para)
 msgid ""
 "If you had used integer precision instead of floating point, the highlights "
-"really would be blown: The sample points would have a maximum channel values "
-"of 255, 65535 or 4294967295, depending on the bit depth. And masking would "
+"really would be blown: The sample points would have a maximum channel values"
+" of 255, 65535 or 4294967295, depending on the bit depth. And masking would "
 "only “recover” a solid expanse of gray, completely lacking any details (try "
 "for yourself and see what happens)."
 msgstr ""
+"Om du hade använt heltalsprecision i stället för flyttal skulle högdagrarna "
+"verkligen vara utbrända: provpunkterna skulle ha maximala kanalvärden på "
+"255, 65535 eller 4294967295, beroende på bitdjupet. Maskning skulle då bara "
+"”återställa” en jämn grå yta helt utan detaljer (prova själv och se vad som "
+"händer)."
 
 #: src/appendix/tone-mapping-tutorial.xml:240(para)
 msgid ""
 "<emphasis role=\"bold\">Add an inverse grayscale layer mask</emphasis>: "
-"Right-click on the layer and select <menuchoice><guimenu>Layer</"
-"guimenu><guisubmenu>Mask</guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Add Layer Masks…</"
-"guimenuitem></menuchoice>, and when the <guilabel>Add Layer Mask</guilabel> "
-"dialog pops up, choose <guilabel>Grayscale copy of layer</guilabel> and "
-"check the <guilabel>Invert mask</guilabel> box."
-msgstr ""
+"Right-click on the layer and select "
+"<menuchoice><guimenu>Layer</guimenu><guisubmenu>Mask</guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Add"
+" Layer Masks…</guimenuitem></menuchoice>, and when the <guilabel>Add Layer "
+"Mask</guilabel> dialog pops up, choose <guilabel>Grayscale copy of "
+"layer</guilabel> and check the <guilabel>Invert mask</guilabel> box."
+msgstr ""
+"<emphasis role=\"bold\">Lägg till en omvänd gråskalelagermask</emphasis>: "
+"högerklicka på lagret och välj "
+"<menuchoice><guimenu>Lager</guimenu><guisubmenu>Mask</guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Lägg"
+" till lagermasker…</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. När dialogrutan "
+"<guilabel>Lägg till lagermask</guilabel> öppnas väljer du "
+"<guilabel>Gråskalekopia av lager</guilabel> och kryssar i "
+"<guilabel>Invertera mask</guilabel>."
 
 #: src/appendix/tone-mapping-tutorial.xml:255(para)
 msgid ""
 "As shown in Figure 5 below, at this point the highlights will be brought "
-"back into the display range, meaning all RGB channel values are between 0.0f "
-"and 1.0f. But the image will probably look a little odd (sort of cloudy and "
-"flat), and depending on the image, the brightest highlights might actually "
+"back into the display range, meaning all RGB channel values are between 0.0f"
+" and 1.0f. But the image will probably look a little odd (sort of cloudy and"
+" flat), and depending on the image, the brightest highlights might actually "
 "have dark splotches—don’t worry! this is temporary."
 msgstr ""
+"Som figur 5 nedan visar förs högdagrarna nu tillbaka till "
+"visningsintervallet, vilket innebär att alla RGB-kanalvärden ligger mellan "
+"0,0f och 1,0f. Men bilden ser troligen lite märklig ut (ungefär molnig och "
+"platt), och beroende på bilden kan de ljusaste högdagrarna ha mörka fläckar "
+"– oroa dig inte, det är tillfälligt."
 
 #: src/appendix/tone-mapping-tutorial.xml:264(emphasis)
 msgid "Figure 5"
@@ -490,6 +566,8 @@
 "Result of adding an inverse grayscale layer mask to bring the highlights "
